```

`@theme inline` re-exports the families as Tailwind font utilities:

```css
@theme inline {
  --font-display: var(--type-family-display);
  --font-body: var(--type-family-body);
  --font-mono: var(--type-family-mono);
}
```

Dark mode (`[data-theme="dark"]`) re-declares the same variable names with dark values — so **the same class names work in both themes**.

### 3.3 How tokens are accessed — the API in one table

| Token kind | CSS var | How you write it in JSX |
|---|---|---|
| Color | `--color-ink-primary` | `text-ink-primary`, `bg-surface-elevated`, `border-border-subtle`, `text-accent-terracotta` |
| Radius | `--radius-card` | `rounded-card`, `rounded-control`, `rounded-subtle`, `rounded-full` |
| Shadow | `--shadow-floating` | `shadow-floating` |
| Spacing | `--spacing-4` | `p-4`, `gap-3`, `mt-2` (4px scale; **no `spacing-5`** — it doesn't exist) |
| Breakpoint | `--breakpoint-md` | `md:`, `lg:` (only 768px and 1024px) |
| Type scale | `--type-scale-headline-md` | `[font:var(--type-scale-headline-md)]` (arbitrary property syntax) |
| Layout width | `--layout-container-max` | `max-w-(--layout-container-max)` (Tailwind v4 CSS-var shorthand) |
| Motion | `--motion-fade-in` | `fade-in` class only |
| Focus ring | `--stroke-focus` | applied globally in `globals.css` `:focus-visible` |

### 3.4 Representative component consuming tokens

`frontend/components/preview/preview-card.tsx`:

```tsx
<article className="flex flex-col gap-3 rounded-card border border-border-subtle bg-surface-elevated px-5 py-4">
  ...
  <p className="[font:var(--type-scale-meta-sm)] text-ink-muted">
  <h3 className="[font:var(--type-scale-headline-sm)] text-ink-primary">
  <p className="[font:var(--type-scale-microtag)] text-ink-muted">
  <button className="rounded-control border border-border-subtle px-4 py-2 [font:var(--type-scale-meta-md)] text-ink-secondary">
```

Note the pattern: **`rounded-card` / `border-border-subtle` / `bg-surface-elevated` for shape+fill; `[font:var(--type-scale-*)]` for type; `text-ink-*` for ink.** Class strings are frequently built with `[...].join(" ")` for conditional variants.

### 3.5 `styles/globals.css` — global bits only

```css
@import "tailwindcss";
@import "./tokens.css";

html, body { margin: 0; background: var(--color-surface-paper); color: var(--color-ink-primary); }
body { font: var(--type-scale-body-md); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }

/* Focus ring: the fourth sanctioned terracotta use. Solid stroke, never a glow. */
:focus-visible { outline: var(--stroke-focus); outline-offset: 2px; }

/* motion.fadeIn: the only transition in the product. @starting-style fades an element in
   when it first renders, without JavaScript. */
.fade-in {
  transition: var(--motion-fade-in);
  @starting-style { opacity: 0; }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .fade-in { transition: none; }
}
```

### 3.6 `styles/tokens.test.ts` — full behavior

This is the **design-token contract test**. It runs in the **node** environment (`// @vitest-environment node`) and **parses `DESIGN.md` itself**.

**The DESIGN.md path is hard-coded in one place:**

```ts
// The one place the dated design-doc path lives.
const DESIGN_MD = path.resolve(
  __dirname,
  "../../_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/ux-designs/ux-EventPulse24-2026-08-23/DESIGN.md",
);
```

So `DESIGN.md` lives at **`_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/ux-designs/ux-EventPulse24-2026-08-23/DESIGN.md`** (repo-relative), *not* at `frontend/DESIGN.md`.

**Aliases it knows about:**

```ts
const ALIASES: Record<string, string> = {
  "color.cool.public": "color.accent.slate",
  "color.ink.meta": "color.ink.muted",
};
```

**The 21 expected color names** (20 primaries + 1 alias) are listed explicitly in `COLOR_NAMES`.

**What it asserts:**

| Suite | Assertion |
|---|---|
| `DESIGN.md parse` | Exactly the 21 color bullets exist, **by name**, in both "### Dark mode (default)" and "### Light mode (alternative)"; the alias `color.cool.public` has the **same value** as `color.accent.slate` in both modes. |
| `tokens.css colors` | Declares exactly **20 `--color-*` variables per mode** (after aliasing); **every value matches DESIGN.md byte-for-byte** (whitespace-normalized, lowercased) in both light and dark; **never declares an alias as its own variable** (e.g. `--color-cool-public:` must not appear). |
| `tokens.css elevation` | `--shadow-floating` is `0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.08)` in light and `...0.4` in dark; `--glow-today` / `--glow-brandmark` are `none` in light and the exact sanctioned glows in dark; `--shadow-*` is `initial` so only `--shadow-floating` exists. |
| `tokens.css shapes, spacing and type` | All **7 radii** from DESIGN.md §Shapes match, and **exactly those** are declared (an extra radius would become a `rounded-*` class); all **11 spacing steps** match and **exactly those** are declared, and `--spacing` is `initial` (**no Tailwind multiplier**); all **3 type families** start with a `next/font` variable then DESIGN.md's fallbacks; only `--breakpoint-md` (768px) and `--breakpoint-lg` (1024px) exist. |
| `theme switching` | **No stylesheet in `styles/` may contain `prefers-color-scheme`** — the theme is chosen, never automatic. |

**Key parsing helpers:**

```ts
const COLOR_BULLET = /^- `(color\.[a-z.]+)` — `([^`]+)`/;
const cssVar = (tokenPath: string) => `--${tokenPath.replaceAll(".", "-")}`;
const norm = (value: string) => value.replace(/\s+/g, "").toLowerCase();
```

The doc comment at the top states the intent:

```ts
/**
 * tokens.css matches DESIGN.md, read from the design doc itself, so a design change fails here
 * until the CSS follows. The parser must find exactly the expected tokens: a reworded or
 * reformatted DESIGN.md fails loudly instead of passing on an empty set.
 */
```

**Implication for `Card.PulseDigest`:** if the component needs a **new** token (e.g. a new radius or a new spacing step), `tokens.css` **and** `DESIGN.md` must both change, or `tokens.test.ts` fails. If the component only consumes existing tokens, no test change is needed.

### 3.7 `styles/motion.test.ts` (also binding)

```ts
it("is the only transition or animation in any stylesheet", () => {
  for (const [file, text] of sheets) {
    const transitions = [...text.matchAll(/^\s*transition:\s*([^;]+);/gm)].map((m) => m[1]);
    expect(transitions.every((v) => v === "var(--motion-fade-in)" || v === "none"), file).toBe(true);
    expect(text, file).not.toMatch(/^\s*animation(-name)?:/m);
    expect(text, file).not.toContain("@keyframes");
  }
});
```

### 3.8 `tests/architecture.test.ts` (also binding on markup)

```ts
it("use no Tailwind animation or transition classes (motion goes through .fade-in)", () => {
  for (const file of tsx) {
    expect(motionClasses(readFileSync(file, "utf8")), path.relative(ROOT, file)).toEqual([]);
  }
});
```

The `MOTION_CLASS` regex catches `animate-*`, `transition*`, `duration-*`, `delay-*`, `ease-*` **anywhere** in a `className` string — including `transition` as a word. **Do not write `transition-*` or `duration-*` classes in the Pulse Card.** The only sanctioned motion class is `fade-in`.

Also enforced: **all files in `app/`, `components/`, `lib/`, `styles/`, `tests/` must be kebab-case** (regex `^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*(?:\.[a-z0-9]+)*$` per path segment). So **`pulse-card.tsx`, not `PulseCard.tsx`**.

And: **no UI kit or animation library may be a dependency** — the forbidden list includes `framer-motion`, `motion`, `react-spring`, `gsap`, `animejs`, `lottie`, `tailwindcss-animate`, `@radix-ui/*`, `@headlessui/*`, `shadcn`, etc.

