## 5. Component conventions

### 5.1 Naming & structure

- **Files:** kebab-case, `.tsx` — `preview-card.tsx`, `personal-events-panel.tsx`, `saved-events-section.tsx`, `brand-topbar.tsx`, `digest-step.tsx`. **Enforced by `tests/architecture.test.ts`.**
- **No `index.tsx` barrels** anywhere in `components/`. Every component is imported by its full path: `import { PreviewCard } from "@/components/preview/preview-card";`
- **Exports:** named exports only (`export function Foo(...)`). No default exports except Next.js route pages (`export default function PreviewPage()`), which is the App Router requirement.
- **Props type:** `export type FooProps = { ... }` when the props type is needed outside; inline `{ ... }` for private subcomponents (e.g. `function EventFitDots({ score, tooltipId }: { score: number; tooltipId: string })`).
- **Doc comments:** every component opens with a block comment explaining *why*, and cites the governing spec by name and section (`AD-12`, `FR-2`, `EXPERIENCE.md §8`, `DESIGN.md`). This is pervasive and clearly the house style.

### 5.2 `"use client"` directives

- `"use client"` is at the **very top of the file, before all imports**, with a blank line after.
- It is added **only** when the component needs state, effects, event handlers, browser APIs, or `next/navigation` hooks.
- Server components have **no directive** and are often `async`.

Examples:
- `"use client"` → `components/preview/preview-card.tsx`, `preview-section.tsx`, `card-skeleton.tsx`, `geo-banner.tsx`, `personal-events-panel.tsx`, `components/onboarding/digest-step.tsx`.
- No directive → `components/brand-topbar.tsx`, `components/saved-events-section.tsx` (async server component), `components/preview/*` others, `app/preview/page.tsx`, `app/page.tsx`.

### 5.3 Prop typing style

```tsx
export type PersonalEventsPanelProps = {
  /** The user's personal events, read by the server component that renders this. */
  events?: PersonalEvent[];
  /**
   * The create sheet's open state, when the caller drives it.
   *
   * The **Add** nav affordance opens the create sheet from outside the panel, so the
   * panel has to accept the state from its caller. Left `undefined`, the panel owns it
   * and its own "Add event" button drives it.
   */
  createOpen?: boolean;
  /** Called when the caller drives the create sheet's open state. */
  onCreateOpenChange?: (open: boolean) => void;
};
```

Conventions:
- Optional props carry `?`, and defaults are applied in the destructuring (`events = []`, `savedNote = null`).
- Callbacks are named `onX`, typed `() => void` or `(value) => void`.
- Every prop gets a `/** ... */` comment, often with the *rationale*.

### 5.4 Accessibility patterns observed

| Concern | Pattern | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Icon-only decoration | `aria-hidden="true"` | `<span aria-hidden="true">⚠ </span>`, dot `<span aria-hidden="true">` |
| Non-text meaning | `aria-label` on the trigger | `aria-label={eventFitLabel(score)}` → "Event Fit 4 of 5" |
| Tooltips | `<span role="tooltip" id>` + `aria-describedby` on the trigger; kept in the DOM, hidden via `invisible` (never `hidden`) | `preview-card.tsx` |
| Sections | `aria-label` on `<section>` | `<section aria-label="Pulse Preview">`, `<section aria-label="Location consent">` |
| Live/loading | `role="status"` + `aria-label` | `<div role="status" aria-label="Loading the preview">` |
| Errors | `role="alert"` | `<p role="alert">Couldn't load the preview. Refresh.</p>` |
| Icon-only buttons | explicit `aria-label` | `aria-label={`Edit ${event.name}`}` |
| Focus | global `:focus-visible { outline: var(--stroke-focus); outline-offset: 2px; }` in `globals.css` | — |
| Colour never sole carrier | stripe/label pairing is **enforced in code** and **asserted in tests** | `PersonalEventRow` comment cites WCAG 1.4.1 |

The `PersonalEventRow` doc comment is the project's clearest statement of the rule:

```tsx
/**
 * One personal event.
 *
 * The warm-personal stripe is **always paired with the visible text label "Personal"** —
 * colour is never the sole carrier of meaning (WCAG 1.4.1). This is the same pairing the
 * design system specifies for the timeline event-block and the digest card; there is no
 * Pulse Card in this item, so the rule is proven here and in the conflict sheet's cards.
 */
function PersonalEventRow({ event, onEdit }: { event: PersonalEvent; onEdit: () => void }) {
  ...
    <span aria-hidden="true" className="h-8 w-[3px] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-warm-personal" />
    <span className="text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[0.08em] text-warm-personal uppercase">
      Personal
    </span>
```

Note: this is the **3px stripe pattern** already in the codebase — `h-8 w-[3px] shrink-0 rounded-full` — with a visible text label beside it. This is the closest existing precedent for the Pulse Card's left-edge stripe.

### 5.5 Data fetching

There is **no TanStack Query, no SWR, no react-query**. Two patterns exist:

**(a) Client island reads in the browser** — `components/preview/preview-section.tsx`:

```tsx
async function readPreview(choice: PreviewChoice): Promise<State> {
  try {
    const response = await api.GET("/api/public/preview", {
      params: { query: previewQuery(choice) },
    });
    return response.data ? { kind: "ready", preview: response.data } : { kind: "failed" };
  } catch {
    return { kind: "failed" };
  }
}
```

State is a **discriminated union**:

```tsx
type State = { kind: "loading" } | { kind: "ready"; preview: Preview } | { kind: "failed" };
```

And the effect uses an **unmount guard**:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  let live = true;
  void (async () => {
    const next = await readPreview(readChoice());
    if (live) setState(next);
  })();
  return () => { live = false; };
}, []);
```

**(b) Server component read** — `components/saved-events-section.tsx` (async, no directive):

```tsx
export async function SavedEventsSection() {
  const { events, omitted } = await readSavedEvents();
  ...
}

async function readSavedEvents(): Promise<SavedEvents> {
  if (!apiBaseUrl()) return { events: [], omitted: 0 };

  try {
    const response = await api.GET("/api/personal/saved-events", {
      headers: await sessionHeaders(),
    });
    return {
      events: response.data?.items ?? [],
      omitted: response.data?.omitted ?? 0,
    };
  } catch {
    return { events: [], omitted: 0 };
  }
}
```

Server-side reads **must forward the visitor's cookies** (`sessionHeaders()` from `lib/session.ts`), because the Next.js server is a separate HTTP client with no session of its own.

### 5.6 Components read in full (for style reference)

- `frontend/components/preview/preview-card.tsx` — quoted in §2.
- `frontend/components/personal-events-panel.tsx` — client island owning create → 409-conflict → resolve → edit; API calls via `api.POST` / `api.PATCH`; error handling via `response.error` (not exceptions).
- `frontend/components/saved-events-section.tsx` — server component; read-only; graceful empty list on failure.
- Also read: `components/preview/card-skeleton.tsx`, `components/preview/geo-banner.tsx`, `components/brand-topbar.tsx`, `components/onboarding/digest-step.tsx`, `lib/session.ts`, `lib/preview-choice.ts`, `lib/timezones.ts`.

